59,"dimensions":60},"Widely spaced, large, wide letters, very neatly and regularly carved with a thin groove. Large omicron, Nu with diagonal fully descending, kappa with near full length arms, epsilon with short middle bar.",[61,67],{"type":62,"l":63,"from":64,"to":64,"h":65,"unit":66,"atLeast":65,"atMost":65},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","120","mm",{"type":68,"l":69,"from":64,"to":70,"unit":66},"interlinear","Interlineation line 1 to 2","line2",{"_":72,"notBefore":73,"notAfter":74,"evidence":75},"4th century BCE (?) ('I caratteri epigrafici possono riportasi almeno al IV sec., circa, se e vero che alla lin.2 non e segnato con l'omega l'aumento del verbo.' Manganaro (however, also observes possible Hieronic parallels)",-400,-251,"lettering",[77,82],{"_":78,"type":79,"ref":80,"region":81},"Syracusae","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462503","Sicilia",{"_":83,"type":84,"ref":85,"region":81},"Siracusa","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2523083",[87],[88,89],37.08415,15.27628,{"_":91,"type":92,"subtype":93,"notAfter":94,"geo":95,"geoCert":98},"Found, before 1885, in the area of the Altar of Hieron; currently in storage in the archaeological park of Neapolis","found","discovered","1885",[96,97],37.0745769,15.2768794,"high",[96,97],{"_":101,"type":102,"subtype":103,"geo":19},"None","observed","autopsied",[],"Sicily",{"_":107,"role":108,"ref":109,"museum":110},"Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/097",{"slug":111,"type":108,"name":107,"uri":109,"description":112,"location":113},"097","An outstanding collection of archaeological material. The collection ranges from Siracusa and the surrounding territory (Megara Hyblaia, Akrai, Kasmenai etc) to encompass all of eastern Sicily, reaching as far as Gela and Agrigento. The ground floor covers prehistory through to the end of the Classical period. Upstairs includes Hellenistic and Roman Syracuse and a display of material from the catacombs. A gallery displaying material from Hellenistic eastern Sicily is in preparation.",{"settlement":83,"region":83,"country":114,"address":115,"geo":116},"Italy","Viale Teocrito 66, 96100 - Siracusa",{"lat":117,"lon":118},37.07636989,15.2866213,{"_":120,"type":121},"3","inventory",{"_":123,"mainLang":124,"languages":125},"Ancient Greek","grc",[123],{"type":127,"bibl":128},"edition",[129,144],{"type":130,"n":131,"date":132,"citedRange":133,"ptr":134,"ref":136,"inscriptionDate":138,"title":139,"author":140,"citation":141,"uri":142,"year":143},"bulletin","SEG","1923-","34.0978",{"target":135},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/F2GG87EQ",{"_":137,"target":137},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796","1984","Supplementum epigraphicum graecum","","\u003Cspan>‘Supplementum Epigraphicum Graecum’, \u003Ci>Supplementum Epigraphicum Graecum\u003C/i>, 1923, \u003Ca href=\"http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/1607583\">http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/1607583\u003C/a>\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/F2GG87EQ","1923",{"author":145,"date":146,"citedRange":147,"ptr":148,"ref":150,"inscriptionDate":146,"title":152,"citation":153,"uri":154,"year":146},"Manganaro","1977","155-156 ph dr",{"target":149},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/JQHZXXJN",{"_":151,"target":151},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001440","Per la storia dei culti nella Sicilia greca","\u003Cspan>Giacomo Manganaro, «Per la storia dei culti nella Sicilia greca», \u003Ci>Cronache di archeologia e di storia dell’arte\u003C/i> 16 (1977): 148–64\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/JQHZXXJN",{"type":156,"bibl":157},"discussion",[19],{"editor":159,"principal":162,"contributors":163,"change":179},{"_":160,"ref":161},"Jonathan Prag","#JP",{"_":160,"ref":161},[164,167,171,175],{"_":160,"xml:id":165,"ref":166},"JP","http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":168,"xml:id":169,"ref":170},"James Cummings","JCu","http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6686-3728",{"_":172,"xml:id":173,"ref":174},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":176,"xml:id":177,"ref":178},"Valentina Mignosa","VM","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511",{"_":180,"when":181,"who":161},"Jonathan Prag revised metadata","2026-09-25",[183],{"atLeast":184,"atMost":184},120,[186,187],"Supplementum epigraphicum graecum, 1923-","Manganaro, 1977, Per la storia dei culti nella Sicilia greca",[189,190],"F2GG87EQ","JQHZXXJN",[192,193,194,21,26,30,195,196,197,198,196,199,200,124],"isic003008","fragment of a monumental greek inscription",{"_":5},"syracusae","siracusa","sicilia","sicily","museo archeologico regionale paolo orsi","ancient greek",{"title":202,"body":203,"divs":204,"editions":223,"images":233,"handnote":234,"deprecation":19},"ISic003008. Fragment of a monumental Greek inscription","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cspan data-text=\"ὶ\">ὶ̣\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"Νύ\">Νύ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">.\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cspan data-text=\"οἰκοδ\">οἰκοδ̣\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cspan data-text=\"τελέ\">τελέ\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cspan data-text=\"ὶ\">.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Νύ\">ΝΥ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">·\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cspan data-text=\"οἰκοδ\">ΟΙΚΟ.\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cspan data-text=\"τελέ\">ΤΕΛΕ\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>Text based on photograph\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"1\">1: \u003Cspan>Manganaro 1977: [Ἀπόλλονι κα]ὶ̣ Νύμ̣[φαις]\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"2\">2: \u003Cspan>Manganaro 1977: [τὸν βομὸν] οἰκοδ̣[όμεσε]\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"3\">3: \u003Cspan>Manganaro 1977: τελέ[ος]\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2> translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Manganaro speculates that the block is part of an altar, at least 3.5m wide, on the basis of his proposed (entirely speculative) restoration of the text. The inventory records the piece as coming from the area of the Great Altar, but no other information is preserved: as inventory no.3, the piece was in the museum at its foundation, but there appears to be no trace of the piece in other documentation (not included in Orsi's initial taccuini in which he recorded most of the initial epigraphic collection, and not seemingly mentioned by Kaibel, nor by the earlier editors such as the Prince of Torremuzza, nor the collection of Cesare Gaetani). The letters are clearly classical or early Hellenistic in form, and monumental, but it remains difficult to say more without further context. There is the very faintest possibility that it is part of the lost text recorded in IG XIV.10, originally reported by Metellus (and which has ΟΙΚΟ in line 2), but this was said to come from the area of the Temple of Zeus Olympios, and the reports do not suggest a text of the size that would have been necessary, so this seems extremely unlikely.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Manganaro 1977 155-156 ph dr \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001440\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001440\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1984 34.0978 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>Widely spaced, large, wide letters, very neatly and regularly carved with a thin groove. Large omicron, Nu with diagonal fully descending, kappa with near full length arms, epsilon with short middle bar.\u003C/p> Line 1  120  Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[205,208,211,214,217,220],{"id":206,"html":207},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"att